 75CO c  2021Es05: {+75}Co source was produced via in-flight fission of E=345   
 75CO2c  MeV {+238}U beam from the RIKEN accelerator complex on a 3-mm-thick    
 75CO3c  {+9}Be target. Fragments were separated by the BigRIPS magnetic        
 75CO4c  spectrometer, selected by |DE-B|r-tof method, and transported through  
 75CO5c  the Zero-Degree spectrometer (ZDS) to the decay station. Charged       
 75CO6c  particles were detected with the WAS3ABi silicon array consisting of 8 
 75CO7c  layers of 1-mm-thick DSSSDs and |g rays were detected with the EURICA  
 75CO8c  array consisting of 84 HPGe crystals. Measured E|g, |g(t). Deduced     
 75CO9c  isomer T{-1/2}, J, |p. Comparisons with theoretical calculations.      
